     1	"""Standalone MelBandRoformer front-end, for kernel-level profiling with nsys.
     2	
     3	Reproduces — with public PyTorch ops only, no repo code on the profiled path —
     4	the exact op chain of MelBandRoformer.forward() up to and including band_split:
     5	
     6	    window       torch.hann_window   regenerated on-device EVERY forward (the model
     7	                                     does this too — watch for it in the trace)
     8	    stft         torch.stft          center-pad (reflect) + framing*window + batched
     9	                                     FFT; the FFT lands in cuFFT library kernels
    10	    view_as_real / merge stereo      complex -> (re, im), stereo folded into freq dim
    11	    band gather  advanced indexing   mel-scaled band grouping via freq_indices;
    12	                                     overlapping bands DUPLICATE frequency bins
    13	    fold complex into freq           permute + copy
    14	    band_split   per-band RMSNorm + Linear(dim_in -> dim), a Python loop over
    15	                                     num_bands skinny matmuls, then stack
    16	
    17	NOTE: this model keeps the complex STFT (re, im) — it never takes magnitude,
    18	and the "mel" is only in how bins are grouped into bands. There is no mel matmul.
    19	
    20	Config matches config/config_aug.yaml — the original/teacher architecture, same
    21	front-end as the public MelBandRoformer vocal checkpoint (provenance-clean for
    22	publication):
    23	    sample_rate 44100, n_fft 2048, hop 441, win 2048, normalized False,
    24	    stereo, num_bands 60, dim 384, chunk_size 352800 (8 s), fp32.
    25	
    26	Profile (only the measured iterations are captured):
    27	
    28	    nsys profile --capture-range=cudaProfilerApi --capture-range-end=stop \
    29	        -o frontend_trace python frontend.py
    30	    nsys stats -r cuda_gpu_kern_sum frontend_trace.nsys-rep
    31	
    32	Sanity check vs the repo model's front-end (imports repo code; run from repo root,
    33	works on CPU too):
    34	
    35	    python frontend.py --sanity
    36	"""
