    52	# Two-tier validation tolerance, keyed by arm class (prereg amendment /
    53	# fix-pass 2026-08-18 — session-owner rationale recorded verbatim below):
    54	#
    55	#   REPLAY class (tight, rtol 1e-4 / atol 1e-5): the only kernel computing
    56	#   different arithmetic from eager is the fused front-end, and its risky
    57	#   reductions accumulate in fp32 on both sides (tl.dot's fp32 accumulator vs
    58	#   cuBLAS's fp32 accumulation); everything downstream of a capture is
    59	#   bitwise-identical binaries — captured, not regenerated — so the tiny
    60	#   perturbation propagates through identical arithmetic with no fresh noise.
    61	#   Replay arms keep the tight gate because B measured bitwise and G's Triton
    62	#   front-end measured within 1e-4 in the 2026-08-17 smoke (fp32 accumulation
    63	#   both sides). D, E and F join this class (D/F: eager variants of the same
    64	#   kernels; E: fused + replay — the same numeric path as G, minus streams).
    65	#
    66	#   RECOMPILED class (loose, rtol 1e-2 / atol 1e-3): fp16 eps ~ 9.77e-4;
    67	#   Inductor legitimately reorders reductions over K <= 512, honest drift
    68	#   ~ sqrt(K)*eps ~ 1e-2 relative; atol governs near-silent stem regions.
    69	#   Divergence is injected at every regenerated kernel and compounds with
    70	#   depth: different reduction trees, different fusion boundaries, fused
    71	#   fp32-register chains rounding in different places than eager's
    72	#   materialized intermediates, and libdevice approximations that don't match
    73	#   eager bit-for-bit.
    74	#
    75	#   CLASSIFICATION RULE (the tier assignment IS this rule, not an arm list):
    76	#   tier = compiler-regenerated kernels present or not. Corrected 2026-09-01:
    77	#   E was initially placed loose from the owner's arm-ledger memory, but
    78	#   repo-E as built is fused-Triton + whole-forward replay of the fp32
    79	#   front-end — NO Inductor-generated kernels on its path — so the rule puts
    80	#   it in the tight tier; the rule outranks the ledger. If the amended prereg
    81	#   later redefines E as an Inductor arm, build_arm_step's E branch and this
    82	#   tier assignment move together under the same rule — flag it then.
    83	VAL_TOL = {                      # arm -> (rtol, atol)
    84	    'A':  (1e-4, 1e-5), 'B':  (1e-4, 1e-5), 'D': (1e-4, 1e-5),
    85	    'E':  (1e-4, 1e-5), 'F':  (1e-4, 1e-5), 'G': (1e-4, 1e-5),
    86	    'C1': (1e-2, 1e-3), 'C2': (1e-2, 1e-3),
