     1	"""Run ONE (arm x regime) measurement in ONE fresh process.
     2	
     3	PREREG: separate OS process per (arm x chunk regime) — scripts/run_all.sh
     4	launches `python arms/run_arm.py` freshly for every run; this file never loops
     5	over arms or regimes.
     6	
     7	    python arms/run_arm.py --arm G --chunk 4410 --tag r1
     8	    python arms/run_arm.py --arm C2 --chunk 352800 --tag outputcode --skip-timing
     9	
    10	Phase order in main() (AUDIT-MAP[1] — the timed region excludes everything
    11	before step 6):
    12	    1 build reference (eager stock FrontEnd, seed 0)
    13	    2 build arm model (same seed — state_dict equality ASSERTED), then the
    14	      arm step: compile (C1/C2) or graph capture (B/E/G) happens here
    15	    3 settle: compile arms run until recompilation stops (logged); other
    16	      arms run a plain warmup loop
    17	    4 validate: >= 2 passes, different data, vs the eager reference
    18	    5 (--skip-timing stops here — used for the C2 output_code reads)
    19	    6 timed region: common.timed_run — prereg 5a latency block (inside the
    20	      cudaProfilerApi capture range) + free-running throughput block
    21	    7 per-iteration times PRINTED and saved; one result JSON written
    22	
    23	A validation FAIL or a build/run error marks the result INVALID in the JSON
    24	and exits 0 — it never kills the session (prereg: does not crash the session).
    25	"""
