     1	# C3 extension execution notes
     2	
     3	The prediction in `PREDICTIONS_EXTENSION_C3.md` remains unchanged.
     4	
     5	## Attempt 1 — direct fields, legacy context
     6	
     7	Code `45274f5`; run `c3_20260915`, generation
     8	`13ae324f-3c27-436f-a533-43469fd5d668`. Eager outputs matched the saved stock
     9	eager outputs exactly for every registered seed. The explicit-field repair
    10	removed `_asdict`, exposing a second graph break: the installed Torch 2.8
    11	legacy `torch.backends.cuda.sdp_kernel` returns an unsupported generator
    12	context. The graph-break gate rejected it before timing. The complete failed
    13	attempt is retained.
    14	
    15	## Attempt 2 — equivalent supported context (recorded before execution)
    16	
    17	Replace the legacy context with `torch.nn.attention.sdpa_kernel`, which the
    18	installed Dynamo explicitly supports. Precompute its enum lists outside the
    19	compiled method from the original configuration. Preserve the legacy API's
    20	enum ordering and its implicit `enable_cudnn=True` default; do not silently
    21	pin to Flash alone. Compare the enabled backend states and restoration under
    22	both APIs before compilation. The external method is checked against the
    23	original AST with only the configuration selection and context call changed.
    24	
    25	This corrects the implementation of the authorized graph-break repair. It
    26	does not change tensor operations, precision, thresholds, or the prediction.
    27	The new attempt has a distinct evidence generation and may use only the
    28	time remaining in the original extension's 3,600-second window. As the owner
    29	confirmed, loose agreement to stock eager qualifies C3 for Phase 1; any tight
    30	disagreement with C1 is reported separately.
    31	
    32	## Attempt 2 result and native-tail compatibility boundary
    33	
    34	Code `65dc05a`, generation `29764068-1927-4392-a3df-5d041a43054a`.
    35	Eager outputs again matched stock exactly on all three seeds. Removing the
    36	attention breaks exposed a full-forward AOT compiler assertion inside the
    37	iSTFT decomposition: `copy_` writes to an internal `permute_357`, while
    38	`assert_functional_graph` requires its destination to be a graph input.
    39	Compilation failed before any accepted timing or trace. No compiler check
    40	was disabled and no result from this attempt is accepted as C3 timing.
    41	
    42	### Attempt 3 plan (recorded before execution)
    43	
    44	Keep the existing native `torch.istft` call opaque through a custom-operator
    45	registration. This registration contains no new GPU kernel or replacement
    46	arithmetic. An external, mechanically checked copy of the public forward
    47	changes only that call's callee. The native return shape, stride, dtype, and
    48	storage offset were inspected on the fixed operating point; the fake
    49	signature is checked by `torch.library.opcheck` and every real invocation.
    50	The native call's host-side checks make it unsafe for CUDA-graph capture, so
    51	its registration declares `cudagraph_unsafe`; no Inductor flag is changed.
    52	The existing C1 compile call decides whether it can use CUDA graphs. Report
    53	that decision explicitly, including any consequence for the prediction.
    54	
    55	This compatibility boundary is an addition to the attention-only repair:
    56	the earlier assumption that that repair alone enables whole-model Inductor
    57	execution was false in the pinned environment. The final C3 arm must be
    58	identified as attention repair **plus native iSTFT boundary**. Preserve both
    59	failed attempts, require eager equivalence and the same baseline validation,
    60	and retain the original extension deadline and all decision thresholds.
    61	
    62	## Attempt 3 result; correction of the compiler-failure diagnosis
    63	
    64	Code `f815538`. The native-iSTFT adapter passed schema/fake-tensor checks and
    65	the full eager model remained exactly equal to stock. Full compilation
    66	failed at the same internal `copy_`, now visibly **before** the opaque iSTFT
    67	call. The initial attribution to iSTFT decomposition was therefore incorrect.
    68	An isolated `index_fill` reproducer using the actual complex shape and
    69	stride produced the same AOT assertion. This identifies the DC-filter
    70	decomposition as the blocker; it is not evidence of an iSTFT bug.
    71	
    72	### Attempt 4 plan (recorded before execution)
    73	
    74	Remove the unnecessary native-iSTFT boundary. Wrap only the original
    75	`Tensor.index_fill` DC-filter call as an opaque operator, with its native
    76	shape, stride, dtype, and storage offset preserved. Restore the public
    77	`torch.istft` call. Mechanically compare the external forward to the pinned
    78	source, allowing just that one callee substitution. Before full-model work,
    79	check schema/fake-tensor behavior, exact native outputs, CUDA-graph capture
    80	and replay, and isolated full-graph compilation. No CUDA-graph-unsafe tag,
    81	compiler flag, backend change, new GPU kernel, or arithmetic rewrite is used.
    82	
    83	The final arm, if qualified, is **attention repair plus native DC-filter
    84	boundary**. Keep all earlier failed attempts and the unchanged prediction.
    85	Every GPU invocation remains inside the first attempt's one-hour window.
    86	
    87	## Attempt 4 result and post-collection tooling
    88	
    89	Measuring code `700c2c6`, generation `b12c7049-f5a5-4f06-881b-59c87fdd9fa4`.
    90	The DC-filter boundary passes its operator checks and eager model checks.
    91	C3 qualifies at the loose tier, settles with zero graph breaks, and completes
    92	unprofiled timing and a node-level trace. The original mapper then rejects
    93	24 dumped SDPA calls versus 12 traced calls: it counted both the cold-cache
    94	and steady graphs. Exact, ordered Triton inventory matching identifies one
    95	steady graph in each process. The temporal parser proves the head-merge
    96	copies from stored values, including kernels named `mm`.
    97	
    98	After collection, the selector and audited ledger replace that invalid
    99	all-dumps mapping in `session.sh`. This changes postprocessing only; the
   100	reported measurements retain the `700c2c6` manifest. The standalone
