     1	# build_spec — standing rules
     2	
     3	Standing engineering rules for this repo (session owner, fix-pass 2026-08-18).
     4	These are binding on every current and future change; reviewers should check
     5	any new code against them. Each rule is stated verbatim, followed by where the
     6	existing code obeys it.
     7	
     8	## Rule 1 — Borrow discipline
     9	
    10	> Borrow discipline: any tensor returned from a graph-replay path is a borrowed
    11	> reference into a reusable buffer. Acquire borrowed references last, convert to
    12	> owned immediately (clone() after the sync), and keep the code window between
    13	> acquisition and clone empty. Never retain replay outputs across iterations
    14	> without cloning.
    15	
    16	Where the code obeys it today:
    17	- `arms/common.py` — `validate()`: `out = step(x)` → `torch.cuda.synchronize()`
    18	  → `out = out.clone()`, with nothing in between; the clone happens before any
    19	  comparison and before the next pass.
    20	- `arms/common.py` — `ReplayBandSplit.forward()` returns the static output
    21	  buffer directly and its docstring marks it as reused; every consumer treats
    22	  it as borrowed.
    23	- The timing loops never retain step outputs at all — only wall times.
    24	
    25	## Rule 2 — Capture is final
    26	
    27	> Capture is final: graph capture is the last thing that happens to a module —
    28	> no .to(), dtype change, or state_dict load after capture; parameter storage
    29	> must not move once a graph holds its pointers.
    30	
    31	Where the code obeys it today:
    32	- `arms/run_arm.py` — order of phases: models are built with
    33	  `build_stock_frontend()` (`.to(device)` + `.eval()` inside), the state_dict
    34	  equality assertion runs on the built models, and only then does
    35	  `build_arm_step()` perform capture (B/E/G). Nothing mutates the module after.
    36	- `arms/common.py` — `_capture_with_fallback()` is the last step of arm
    37	  construction; validation and timing only call the returned step closure.
    38	
    39	A violation of either rule is a correctness bug even if every test passes —
    40	the failure modes (stale borrowed buffers; a graph replaying into freed or
    41	moved storage) are silent.

