Computed at the 100 ms regime, on arm G: R = median wall-time / GPU-busy-time (busy from nsys kernel sum,
same run).
R ≤ ~1.25 → gaps closed by overlap+replay; launch-collapse headroom is small. Candidate (a)'s quantitative
case resizes to wave-quantization + reuse + the deleted stack copy; the categorical (representational-gap)
story carries the claim.
R ≥ ~1.5 → measured headroom stands; grouped kernel has a quantitative target.
Between → gray zone; the week-4 gate weighs it against candidate-(b) evidence.
Structural criterion, independent of timing: if the best generic arm's trace still shows the ~60 separate GEMM
kernels per pass, the categorical claim is confirmed by inspection regardless of wall-time.
